   "class": "other",
   "file": "plugins/specclaw-fleet/lib/podspec.sh",
   "fp": "788fc1082522",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 112,
   "message": "`bundle_subpath` lowercases only the host. Azure DevOps org and project names are case-insensitive, so `https://dev.azure.com/Acme/P/_git/r` and `https://dev.azure.com/acme/p/_git/r` get different bundle folders, and a retry dispatched with the other casing silently misses the saved bundle. The README warns about the host form only. Fix: either fold case for the AzDO org and project segments, or extend the README warning to cover casing.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
